{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/573804-forsaking-the-pure","id":573804,"title":"Forsaking the Pure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-30T05:44:01-07:00","id":573804,"title":"Forsaking the Pure","content":"In a game I'm running, I've achieved something that I thought would be impossible: I got the party to care about a villain NPC. To be fair, he's the scrappy &quot;omega&quot; of the nearby Fire-Touched pack. Blood of the Fox, kind of a selfish, lazy dick. But also stuck in a bad place: he really only pays lip service to the service of Rabid Wolf, and he doesn't like any of his packmates (and the alpha scares the bajeesus out of him).<br /> <br /> He's had a rocky relationship with the players as well: They've targeted him as the weak point in the enemy pack in their ongoing territorial disputes: hacking his phone, following him around, stuff like that. Being a coward, he folds quickly when they intimidate him.<br /> <br /> However, during the last session, one of the PCs made a genuine attempt to open up to the guy when they thought he may have been physically abused by his packmates. With a very frank &quot;Look, obviously we don't like each other, and it makes me feel kind of gross just to tell you this at all, but are you okay?&quot; It took me aback that the players were reaching out to this character like that. Then she gave him her phone number and a warning not to call it unless there was an emergency.<br /> <br /> After that scene, the pack's loremaster turns to me and asks &quot;Is it possible to rebrand a Pure?&quot; and everybody started talking about the possibility of &quot;rescuing&quot; him from the Fire-Touched.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, I've never been more taken aback or proud that my players are taking this angle, especially given that he's attacked them in the past.<br /> <br /> So my question is this: <u><b>What kind of ritual/quest would you make up in order to rebrand a Pure?</b></u> I figure some sort of vision quest through the Flesh and the <i>hisil</i>, interacting with Lunes, and a physical ritual involving either molten silver or mercury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T06:30:26-07:00","id":573867,"title":"","content":"Well officially there's no way to make a pure werewolf forsaken but the story hooks for at least two lodges include it as an option.<br /> <br /> So by default I'd say epic quest time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T06:37:00-07:00","id":573872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/573804-forsaking-the-pure?p=573867#post573867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So by default I'd say epic quest time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah! An epic quest delving into the worlds of the Lunes in order to move Luna giving the character his auspice back.<br /> <br /> In a similar case in my 1e chronicle of years past the &quot;rescued&quot; character was not made a Forsaken again, because the pack didn't find a way to do it. So they took the young, tortured werewolf under their protection, nursed her and gave her light duties in service to the pack, in order to help her buld up self-confidence again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6226-rulandor","name":"Rulandor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T07:44:57-07:00","id":573954,"title":"","content":"The Lodge of the Second Moonrise, IIRC, will symbolically allow someone to become a Rahu, Pure included. He may not have the brands, but the Ralunim may recognize him as one of the auspice, at least. Again, I'm only quoting this from memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T08:27:30-07:00","id":573979,"title":"","content":"Seek out the <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Lodge_of_Salvation\" target=\"_blank\">Lodge of Salvation</a>, from Lodges the Faithful, convince them to perform the Rite of the Silver Scar, which removes the Pure brands and allows a werewolf to become a Forsaken again and join one of the Forsaken tribes, or stay independent as a Ghost Wolf. That part should be easy, since their entire thing is converting the Pure, and usually they don't have willing members to work with.<br /> <br /> There is currently no way to regain an auspice blessing, so presumably if they wanted that back they'd have to find out what auspice they originally were and undergo some quest or another, perhaps trying to impress or otherwise do great deeds before their old auspice' lunes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-30-2015, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T08:40:10-07:00","id":574002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/573804-forsaking-the-pure?p=573979#post573979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seek out the <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Lodge_of_Salvation\" target=\"_blank\">Lodge of Salvation</a>, from Lodges the Faithful, convince them to perform the Rite of the Silver Scar, which removes the Pure brands and allows a werewolf to become a Forsaken again and join one of the Forsaken tribes, or stay independent as a Ghost Wolf. That part should be easy, since their entire thing is converting the Pure, and usually they don't have willing members to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, getting the character to become willing will be a plotline in and of itself, and I can tell you right now that if anybody says to him, &quot;We could see about getting your brands back!&quot; this early on in the process it's going to send him right back to square one: he still sees the brands as symbols of Luna's tyranny and his lack of brands as proof that he is free. Of course, his place as omega in a Fire-Touched pack makes him think that his &quot;freedom&quot; is an illusion.<br /> <br /> It'll be fun to see how this goes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T09:14:47-07:00","id":574021,"title":"","content":"The Lodge of Salvation does mostly specialize in the 'deprogramming' of young Pure. They have another rite that sort of blocks them from sight so they'll have time to work on the potential convert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T11:55:56-07:00","id":574154,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Lodge of Salvation would now become a Blood Talon thing? What with the favored prey list going on? I wonder how that would change things...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:02:33-07:00","id":574156,"title":"","content":"Had lots of fun with story hooks concerning deprogramming the Pure. One of the pcs of my first Werewolf game ended up <i>creating </i>the Lodge of Salvation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:34:07-07:00","id":574203,"title":"","content":"As far as details, I'm thinking a confrontation with one of each kind of Lune is in order, as well as a deed worthy of each kind of renown, and some sort of sacrament or material that's thematically related, plus a solvent to mix those materials in based on silver. And a ton of Essence. For the &quot;tangible&quot; component of the brands, it's practically a tattoo fetish empowered by the Lunes/Luna. The ritemaster should preferably be the same auspice as the Pure used to be, or the appropriate Lune (in this case, an Irraka/Irralunim).<br /> <br /> The Forsaken-to-be doesn't <i>need</i> to be accompanied by a pack on this quest, but it would probably be helpful in a practical sense as well as being able to hit some of those renown deeds (being a part of a pack is integral, methinks). Still, if the PCs in <i>my</i> case decide to go with him they can help him out and make sure he stays the course: being a lazy coward, he'll need the support.<br /> <br /> Naturally, leaving their territory would be a problem, and further emphasize their willingness to help the Pure.<br /> <br /> Of course, are they really helping him, or just recruiting him into their own cult-like ideology? If the Forsaken-to-be will just end up being a Ghost Wolf anyway, this probably isn't the sort of quest that he'd want to go on. This story has so many good questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:42:28-07:00","id":574229,"title":"","content":"I had defecting to the forsaken be a bit easier than that. Rite of renunciation first, and another rite to remove pure renown brands. If you were never forsaken before (meaning the pure did that rite that hides you from luna before you changed and you didn't join the pure by tearing away your auspice) you get the auspice you were supposed to have when the right moon phase next comes around.<br /> <br /> The reason it's hard is because the pure will try to interupt the process by whatever means necessary.<br /> <br /> Now, if you did undergo the rite of blood and silver, then that's another story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:53:23-07:00","id":574238,"title":"","content":"I forgot that the Pure have a way to keep you from becoming a Forsaken during your First Change. That's what I get for not reading the Pure book all the way through. Or retaining it very well after 2E dropped. Whoops.<br /> <br /> I had been assuming that all of the Pure had undergone the Rite of Blood and Silver, willingly or otherwise. We'll have to see what I can do with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}